#: ../../../tutorials/07-intro-to-async.md:186
msgid "Borrowed Inputs and Spawn Safety"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/07-intro-to-async.md:188
msgid ""
"Kernel `&Tensor` params accept three input forms: `Tensor<T>`, "
"`Arc<Tensor<T>>`, and `&Tensor<T>`. Borrowed inputs (`&Tensor<T>`) work with "
"`.sync_on()` and `.await`, but the compiler rejects them with `tokio::spawn`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/07-intro-to-async.md:192
msgid ""
"let weights: Tensor<f32> = api::ones(&[1024]).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"\n"
"// OK — borrow is contained in the sync call.\n"
"let result = my_kernel(out, &weights).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"\n"
"// OK — borrow checker ensures weights outlives the await.\n"
"let result = my_kernel(out, &weights).await?;\n"
"\n"
"// COMPILE ERROR — &weights is not 'static, so the future can't be spawned.\n"
"let handle = tokio::spawn(my_kernel(out, &weights).into_future());\n"
"//                                       ^^^^^^^^ borrowed value does not "
"live long enough\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/07-intro-to-async.md:206
msgid ""
"This is enforced at compile time by Rust's lifetime system. If you need to "
"spawn, use `Arc<Tensor<T>>` instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/07-intro-to-async.md:209
msgid ""
"let weights: Arc<Tensor<f32>> = api::ones(&[1024]).sync_on(&stream)?."
"into();\n"
"let handle = tokio::spawn(my_kernel(out, weights).into_future());  // OK — "
"Arc is 'static\n"
msgstr ""

